{0 lwt_multicore}

Communication between Lwt loops running on different domains.

Lwt promises are domain-local: a promise belongs to the loop that created it, and
touching one from another domain raises rather than corrupting it quietly. That is
what makes several independent loops safe, and it is also why they need something to
talk through. This package is that something.

Everything here returns an ordinary local promise, resolved by the calling loop.
Nothing crosses a domain except plain data and the wake-up that carries it. What
tells you a value is shared is its {e type}, not the way you use it: the code around
a {!Lwt_multicore.Mutex.t} looks like ordinary Lwt.

It is a separate opam package so that its [saturn] dependency stays out of [lwt],
whose OCaml 4.14 floor and js_of_ocaml support must not be touched by it. It
requires OCaml 5.

For how to run several loops in the first place, and for what belongs to which loop,
see the section "Several loops, one per domain" of the Lwt manual.

{1 API}

{!modules:
Lwt_multicore
}
